<title>DENMARK: Danish Sept trade surplus 3.181 billion DKK.</title>
<headline>Danish Sept trade surplus 3.181 billion DKK.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark posted a trade surplus excluding ships of 3.181 billion crowns in September 1996 compared to a revised 2.749 billion crowns in August 1996, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH TRADE (billions of crowns):</p>
<p>			     Sept 1996    August 1996  Sept 1995</p>
<p> Exports			 24.983	23.126	24.656</p>
<p> Imports			 21.824	20.165	21.173</p>
<p> Trade balance		  3.159	 2.962	 3.483</p>
<p> Trade balance excl ships   3.181	 2.749	 3.368</p>
<p> Seasonally adjusted	  1.982	 2.667	 2.229</p>
<p>balance excluding ships</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast an average September trade surplus excluding ships of 3.4 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33969650</p>
</text>
